I continue walking across the flea market.
I stop at a table with old electronics.
There are many cameras here.
I pick up a silver camera.
"Excuse me, how much does this camera cost?" I ask the seller.
"This camera costs forty euros," he says.
I point to another camera.
"And that camera back there?"
"That one costs sixty euros," he answers.
"That one is still in very good condition."
I look at the cameras closely.
I do not really need a camera at all.
"They are really very beautiful," I say.
"But I bought my digital camera many years ago."
The seller smiles warmly.
"Old things have more character, though," he says.
I laugh and put the silver camera back onto the table.
"You are right about that," I answer.
The short conversation is really nice.
But I prefer just looking today anyway.
